  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Original fossil-shell target retained: inflated smooth oval cowrie, anterior extension of the aperture as a short channel, and long toothed ventral slit. Not a living animal and not a generic unbroken oval pebble. [\"Three real views are sufficient for low-poly external morphology, not exact internal anatomy or a watertight museum scan\", \"Photographic perspective gives approximate dimensions and intermediate surfaces require modest interpolation\", \"Bone-beige fossil palette is artistic neutral coloration, not evidence of the living shell pattern\"] {\"units\": \"metres\", \"target_length\": 0.066, \"target_width\": 0.037, \"target_depth\": 0.034, \"tolerance_fraction\": 0.12, \"source\": \"PRI69852 image has an actual 3cm line approximately184px. Long shell ~407px, width~227px and end-view height~210px imply approximately66x37x34mm. Pixel/projection estimates, not caliper measurements.\", \"separate_comparison\": \"PRI76742 is another specimen stated ~8cm by PRI. It is contextual corroboration only and must NOT replace PRI69852 scale or locality.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Original fossil-shell target retained: inflated smooth oval cowrie, anterior extension of the aperture as a short channel, and long toothed ventral slit. Not a living animal and not a generic unbroken oval pebble. [\"Three real views are sufficient for low-poly external morphology, not exact internal anatomy or a watertight museum scan\", \"Photographic perspective gives approximate dimensions and intermediate surfaces require modest interpolation\", \"Bone-beige fossil palette is artistic neutral coloration, not evidence of the living shell pattern\"] {\"units\": \"metres\", \"target_length\": 0.066, \"target_width\": 0.037, \"target_depth\": 0.034, \"tolerance_fraction\": 0.12, \"source\": \"PRI69852 image has an actual 3cm line approximately184px. Long shell ~407px, width~227px and end-view height~210px imply approximately66x37x34mm. Pixel/projection estimates, not caliper measurements.\", \"separate_comparison\": \"PRI76742 is another specimen stated ~8cm by PRI. It is contextual corroboration only and must NOT replace PRI69852 scale or locality.\"}"
  },
